			"notes": {
				"rationale": "Whatever has to go out today leaves the office, away from the speaker, so raus is the Shorthand of hinaus, not a Variant spelling of heraus (de/raus-is-heraus-or-hinaus). Der Zahn muss raus is the minimal pair, with heraus. No motion verb stands in the bracket, and the modal takes no particle, so raus is an ADV target of its own."
